<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">set prompt</ansi> / <ansi fg="command">set fprompt</ansi>

The <ansi fg="command">set prompt</ansi> and <ansi fg="command">set fprompt</ansi> commands let you customize your
in-game prompt. The fight prompt (<ansi fg="command">fprompt</ansi>) appears during combat.

<ansi fg="yellow">Usage: </ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">set prompt [default/none]</ansi>       - Reset to default or hide prompt
  <ansi fg="command">set prompt [prompt text]</ansi>        - Set a custom prompt

  <ansi fg="command">set fprompt</ansi>                     - Show current fight prompt & toggle states
  <ansi fg="command">set fprompt default</ansi>             - Reset custom string AND all toggles
  <ansi fg="command">set fprompt [prompt text]</ansi>       - Set fully custom fight prompt (overrides toggles)
  <ansi fg="command">set fprompt tog <name></ansi>          - Toggle individual fight prompt elements on/off


<ansi fg="yellow">Fight Prompt Toggles: </ansi>

  Type <ansi fg="command">set fprompt tog <name></ansi> to turn an element on or off. All are ON by default.

  <ansi fg="magenta">bars</ansi>          HP/SP/CP vital bars
  <ansi fg="magenta">pos</ansi>           Your combat position (hidden when standing)
  <ansi fg="magenta">target</ansi>        Target name
  <ansi fg="magenta">targethealth</ansi>  Target health description (healthy/bruised/wounded/etc)
  <ansi fg="magenta">targetpos</ansi>     Target's current combat position
  <ansi fg="magenta">tank</ansi>          Party front-rank tank name and health bar

  Example: <ansi fg="command">set fprompt tog tank</ansi>  → hides the tank block when soloing


<ansi fg="yellow">Custom Prompt Tokens: </ansi>

  <ansi fg="196">C</ansi><ansi fg="226">o</ansi><ansi fg="46">l</ansi><ansi fg="51">o</ansi><ansi fg="21">r</ansi><ansi fg="201">s</ansi><ansi fg="017">:</ansi>
  <ansi fg="magenta">{fg#:bg#}</ansi> Color, where fg# and bg# are numeric color codes.
            Example: "<ansi fg="109">{46:196}Hello world</ansi>" would look like <ansi fg="46" bg="196">Hello world</ansi>
            See <ansi fg="command">help colors</ansi> for all color codes.
            Note: Only one # (as in <ansi fg="109">{109}</ansi>) it is assumed to be a fg color.
                  You can specify only the bg color as follows: <ansi fg="109">{:bg#}</ansi>

  <ansi fg="health-100">Health:</ansi>
    <ansi fg="magenta">{hp}</ansi>    Current Health - With coloring (see <ansi fg="command">help health</ansi>)
    <ansi fg="magenta">{hp:-}</ansi>  Current Health
    <ansi fg="magenta">{HP}</ansi>    Current Maximum Health - With coloring (see <ansi fg="command">help health</ansi>)
    <ansi fg="magenta">{HP:-}</ansi>  Current Maximum Health
    <ansi fg="magenta">{hp%}</ansi>   Percent of Health left - With coloring (see <ansi fg="command">help health</ansi>)
    <ansi fg="magenta">{hp%:-}</ansi> Percent of Health left

  <ansi fg="mana-100">Conviction:</ansi>
    <ansi fg="magenta">{mp}</ansi>    Current Conviction - With coloring (see <ansi fg="command">help conviction</ansi>)
    <ansi fg="magenta">{mp:-}</ansi>  Current Conviction
    <ansi fg="magenta">{MP}</ansi>    Current Maximum Conviction - With coloring (see <ansi fg="command">help conviction</ansi>)
    <ansi fg="magenta">{MP:-}</ansi>  Current Maximum Conviction
    <ansi fg="magenta">{mp%}</ansi>   Percent of Conviction left - With coloring (see <ansi fg="command">help conviction</ansi>)
    <ansi fg="magenta">{mp%:-}</ansi> Percent of Conviction left

  <ansi fg="8">Vital Bars (fight prompt):</ansi>
    <ansi fg="magenta">{hpbar}</ansi>        Health bar (10-block color bar)
    <ansi fg="magenta">{stbar}</ansi>        Stamina bar (10-block color bar)
    <ansi fg="magenta">{cvbar}</ansi>        Conviction bar (10-block color bar)

  <ansi fg="8">Combat Info (fight prompt):</ansi>
    <ansi fg="magenta">{pos}</ansi>          Your combat position (empty when standing)
    <ansi fg="magenta">{target}</ansi>       Your current target's name
    <ansi fg="magenta">{targethealth}</ansi> Target health: healthy/bruised/wounded/badly wounded/near death/dead
    <ansi fg="magenta">{targetpos}</ansi>    Target's combat position
    <ansi fg="magenta">{tank}</ansi>         Party front-rank tank's name
    <ansi fg="magenta">{tankpos}</ansi>      Tank's combat position
    <ansi fg="magenta">{tankbar}</ansi>      Tank's health bar

  <ansi fg="8">Other:</ansi>
    <ansi fg="magenta">{tp}</ansi>    Unspent Training Points   <ansi fg="magenta">{sp}</ansi>    Unspent Stat Points
    <ansi fg="magenta">{i}</ansi>     Items carried count       <ansi fg="magenta">{I}</ansi>     Maximum carry capacity
    <ansi fg="magenta">{g}</ansi>     Gold on hand              <ansi fg="magenta">{h}</ansi>     Hidden/Invisible flag
    <ansi fg="magenta">{t}</ansi>     Day/Night symbol (<ansi fg="night">☾</ansi>/<ansi fg="day">☀️</ansi>)    <ansi fg="magenta">{T}</ansi>     Full time of day
    <ansi fg="magenta">{ap}</ansi>    Action Points             <ansi fg="magenta">{w}</ansi>     Wait rounds (fprompt)
    <ansi fg="magenta">{enc}</ansi>   Encumbrance tier (light/moderate/heavy/overburdened/crushed)
    <ansi fg="magenta">{casting}</ansi> While casting: spell name and fold progress. Empty when idle.
    <ansi fg="magenta">{\n}</ansi>    New Line

The default prompt is:
<ansi fg="246">{8}[{t} {T} {255}HP:{hp}{8}/{HP} {255}MP:{13}{mp}{8}/{13}{MP}{8}]{239}{h}{8}:</ansi>

The default fight prompt is assembled automatically from your toggle settings.
Use <ansi fg="command">set fprompt default</ansi> to restore all defaults at any time.

<ansi fg="red">Note:</ansi> A custom fprompt string (set with <ansi fg="command">set fprompt <text></ansi>) overrides the toggle
system entirely. Use <ansi fg="command">set fprompt default</ansi> to return to toggle-driven mode.

